id: pm-brief-action-prerequisites
title: Compose a compact prerequisite brief for one intended native action
description: "Combine SDK command contracts, item readiness and declared evidence for an explicitly selected native command and item. Compose authoritative core facts without duplicating validators or selecting work."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-27T04:25:34.000Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T04:52:46.030Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "One call identifies missing close fields and unresolved prerequisites; Satisfied fields are references without repeated bodies; Read-only previews perform zero mutations and carry typed unsupported-capability refusals with remedies; Typed SDK and CLI emit bounded TOON/JSON; docs, non-git public-data validation and npm/Bun release evidence are recorded"
comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T04:25:48.456Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked against pinned SDK public contracts/actionability/lifecycle/schema declarations, core command discovery, pm-lint quality rules and pm-evidence selectors, plus existing tracker items and upstream issue search. Core owns native command availability, lifecycle admission and configured status semantics; pm-lint owns quality diagnosis; pm-evidence owns evidence collection. This feature composes those facts for one explicit action and item, without selecting work, applying actions or creating a second validator. No existing action prerequisite item or GitHub issue found. Plan: typed bounded preview, native command registration, strict shared request schema, reference-only satisfied evidence, non-git and no-write regressions, public-copy measurement, packed install matrix and CI npm/Bun gates. Import/export/sync and journal mutation paths are outside this read-only feature; existing paths remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-27T04:31:37.604Z",codex-agent,"Implementation now composes getContracts availability, certified complete-list reads, resolveItemBlockers (including reverse/external/missing edges), runtime status roles, computeActionabilityReport, native transition evaluation, workflow policy evaluation and SDK lifecycle completeness presets. Satisfied evidence is item/input JSON Pointer references, never copied bodies. Validation found that cold native certified reads initialize derived runtime metadata caches; item/schema/history bytes remain unchanged. Warm repeated previews also preserve all runtime bytes. This distinction will be explicit in measured evidence rather than claiming the SDK performs no derived cache IO."
  "2026-10-27T04:41:28.338Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: replacing only buildActionPrerequisiteBrief with a no-op empty ready preview makes the combined prerequisite regression fail with exit 1; restoring the implementation passes that exact regression with exit 0. Focused suite passed 9/9 including 500 seeded random sequences on a native non-git tracker; parser/output numeric checks, native status roles, old-request replays, SDK read-back state and native competing writes are exercised. Public origin/main snapshot 04b258644a746d289455d1287dd84b5bafe6aa1a: 98 certified items/previews, 115 missing inputs, 277 satisfied references, 0 unresolved references in this corpus, 1486 maximum JSON bytes, 808 maximum conservative tokens, 97601ms elapsed, 0 tracker byte changes under physical read-only permissions. Details and source fingerprint are in docs/action-validation.md. Rechecked SDK staged mutation preview APIs as well: they execute disposable mutations and do not expose a read-only aggregate of missing action inputs; this composition uses public fact/policy readers instead."
  "2026-10-27T04:43:21.456Z",codex-agent,"Local TypeScript source/tests and docstring lint pass (15 files, 183 documented declarations); diff whitespace is clean. Native command argument metadata and singleton read-output declaration are registered. The mandatory linked combined regression is kept targeted for the saturated host; a broader linked attempt reached its default 120-second timeout, while the independent 500-sequence focused suite passed with a longer explicit allowance. Full release and packed matrix evidence will come from CI, with unchanged coverage thresholds. Bun global isolation was smoke-verified using disposable global directory/bin environment coordinates; no executable or SDK is located via argv/which/symlink heuristics."
  "2026-10-27T04:44:45.002Z",codex-agent,"PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-brief/pull/189 is ready for review. Current deterministic action/renderer checks pass 9/9, with new action.ts measured at 100% lines, 99.07% branches and 100% functions; the pm-linked combined regression passes 1/1. Source/test typechecks, docstring lint and changelog check pass. Full npm and Bun release gates are queued at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-brief/actions/runs/40451376112 on commit 62bb8f1bf9a07a852d9e856276e2e42195412c3e; final counts will be reported on the PR after the final head passes. No item is closed, merged or released to a registry."
  "2026-10-27T04:52:44.050Z",codex-agent,"Packed acceptance now resolves the current stable public CLI version for both disposable global scenarios, while project-local npm/Bun cases retain the repository development pin and the minimum-host case retains the declared peer floor. This verifies the current global host without a dependency bump. The earlier queued CI head is superseded only for this validation correction; no native action implementation changed."
